    "status": "present",
    "value": "Group tree nodes by column, order each column by row, and sort equal-row/column collisions by node value. The approach is: coordinate every node, then sort column,row,value with exact collision ordering. Its target cost is O(n log n) time/O(n) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
